name: __PROJECT_NAME__-development
description: Extend the __PROJECT_NAME__ Maximus backend using its optional file conventions.
---

Read CLAUDE.md and the installed Maximus skill. Configure the application in maximus.config.ts.
Add one file per route and method to routes/v1/ (tasks/index.get.ts, tasks/[taskId].delete.ts), each
default-exporting defineHandler from @arbol-ai/maximus with strict input/output schemas; declare a scope or
effect only where the method's default is wrong, and MCP/RPC exposure explicitly. MCP-only tools are
defineTool modules in mcp/tools/. Use optional src/ for
named domain functions. Middleware is discovered in filename order: defineMiddleware wraps requests;
defineOperationMiddleware applies policy after authentication across transports. Keep principal-based
policy in the operation phase. Read the Maximus project-structure guide before adding another module kind.
Build reconciliation owns .maximus/; never edit generated entries. Cloud resources and SQL remain explicit.
Run bun run verify for non-test validation. Tests require a human request.

Vite+ owns the root toolchain: `vite.config.ts` configures lint/format, `vp check` checks them,
`vp build` bundles the Worker and `vp dev` runs it locally. TypeScript and Cloudflare type generation
remain part of `bun run verify`. Tests are never part of automatic deployment.
